 cap</a> to go past the World Cup winning captain and set a new benchmark, =
one that he has held for over 37 years. On Thursday night at Wembley, barri=
ng an unforeseen hamstring twang in the warm-ups, Harry Kane will go past S=
hilton=E2=80=99s final tally of 125 and <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial=
